Find the inverse Laplace transforms (a) L^-1{2s / (s^2 + 1)^2}, (b) L^-1{1 / \surds}

A. t sin t, (1 / \surd\pi)  ullet (1 / \surdt)
B. cos t, (1 / \surd\pi) \cdot t e^{-t^2}
C. e^t sin t, (1 / 2\surd\pi) \cdot t
D. t cos t, (1 / \surd\pi)  ullet (1 / \surdt)
E. t^2 sin t, (1 / 2\surd\pi) \cdot (1 / \surdt)
F. t tan t, (1 / \surd\pi)  ullet (1 / \surdt)
G. t^2 e^t, (1 / 2\surd\pi) \cdot e^{-t^2}
H. t sec t, (1 / \surd\pi)  ullet (1 / \surdt)
I. e^t cos t, (1 / \surd\pi) \cdot t^2
J. sin t, (1 / \surd\pi) \cdot e^{-t^2}

Give your final answer as a single option letter on the last line, in the form Final answer: A.

Suppose that, for some angles $x$ and $y$,

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \sin ^{2} x+\cos ^{2} y=\frac{3}{2} a \\
& \cos ^{2} x+\sin ^{2} y=\frac{1}{2} a^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Determine the possible value(s) of $a$.

Give one exact integer, finite decimal or rational number on the last line, in the form Final answer: -3/2. Do not put an expression or multiple answers on that line.
